Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

Framework: **MSTest 4.1.0** · Integration marker: `[TestCategory("Integration")]`
All 19 smells evaluated; 15 are clean.

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH 1 — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test (testsmells.org #3)
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // ← hard-coded 3-second wall-clock delay
```

**Integration calibration:** Even in integration suites, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell. It makes CI flaky under load (the delay may be too short) and unconditionally slows the suite by 3 s per run. The method is also `async Task` yet uses synchronous `Thread.Sleep`, blocking a thread pool thread.

**Fix — use a polling wait with timeout:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var timeout = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5);
    var interval = TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(100);
    var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
    while (sw.Elapsed < timeout)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(interval);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the timeout period.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; 3 s of wasted wall-clock time per run.

---

### 🔴 HIGH 2 — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org #1)
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

Only one branch ever executes per run, so one assertion path is permanently untested. A data-driven user inserted as a regular `User` will always take the `else` path, meaning the `PremiumUser` assertion is dead code.

**Fix — split into two explicit test methods:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.15m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com");

    Assert.IsInstanceOfType<PremiumUser>(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(((PremiumUser)loaded).DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden testing gap — one branch is likely never exercised, providing false coverage.

---

### 🔴 HIGH 3 — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Unknown Test / Empty Test (testsmells.org #4)
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion — passes even if every row is silently dropped
}
```

The method name suggests "runs without errors" (implicit no-exception assertion), but the framework only catches unhandled exceptions. Silent data corruption or no-op inserts would pass.

**Fix — assert on observable outcome:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    const int count = 100;
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    Assert.AreEqual(count, _repository.ListAll().Count,
        "Not all bulk-inserted users were persisted.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate with zero verification of behavior.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM 4 — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette (testsmells.org extended catalog)
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);          // which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions with no message parameters. When any one fails, the MSTest output shows only the assertion type and values — the developer must open the source to understand *why*.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Persisted name should match.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Persisted email should match.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis in CI — failure messages require source-code lookup.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining **4 tests** are well-designed:

| Test | Notes |
|------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, 2 focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single-purpose with a clean null-check assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | `Assert.AreEqual(3, ...)` is contextually obvious (3 items just inserted) — not a Magic Number smell |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, single clear assertion, 10 is self-documenting |

The `[TestInitialize]`/`[TestCleanup]` setup is tight — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test, so **General Fixture** does not apply. The in-memory SQLite database is hermetic, so **Mystery Guest** does not apply despite using a real database (no external resource dependency). No tests are skipped (**Ignored Test** clean), no `try`/`catch` blocks (**Exception Handling** clean), no `ToString()` comparisons (**Sensitive Equality** clean).

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | Low | Add `Assert.AreEqual(count, ...)` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | Medium | Split into 2 tests per type branch |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | Medium | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-wait loop |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | Low | Add message strings to all 4 assertions |

Fixes 1 and 4 are one-liners. Fix 2–3 require small refactors. Prioritize **#1** first — an assertion-free test is the highest-risk item because it provides zero defect detection while appearing green.
